<div class="script-box">The TSX gave back a small piece of Friday''s record gain Monday, mostly because gold miners cooled off after a concentrated rally and energy names stayed under pressure from oversupplied oil markets. Meanwhile Wall Street set fresh records on renewed AI sector buying, which is a sector rotation story more than a signal that Canadian equities are falling behind structurally. There was also a shipping incident in the Strait of Hormuz overnight, and oil prices have barely reacted, which tells us the supply picture is currently the dominant force in energy pricing, not the headline risk.</div>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
